{"id": "185127", "name": "a.iii composition (paths as formulas)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "functions": [{"name": "f1", "params": ["t"], "body": "f1"}, {"name": "f2", "params": ["t"], "body": "f2"}, {"name": "f3", "params": ["t"], "body": "f3"}], "questiontext": "<p dir=\"ltr\">Let \\(f(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\) Here is the graph of \\(f(x,y)\\):</p>\n<p><img class=\"img-responsive atto_image_button_left\" src=\"data/185127/files/1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"258\" height=\"250\" /></p>\n<p>Three functions \\(\\alpha_i:[a,b] \\rightarrow R^2\\) are given by their formulas below. Match each one with the number of the graph of its composition with \\(f(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\).</p>\n<p>(Please answer with 1, 2 or 3)</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(\\alpha_1(t)=({{CT:1}}, {{CT:2}})\\)</p>\n<p>Graph number of \\(f(\\alpha_1(t))\\): [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(\\alpha_2(t)=({{CT:3}}, {{CT:4}})\\)</p>\n<p>Graph number of \\(f(\\alpha_2(t))\\): [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(\\alpha_3(t)=({{CT:5}}, {{CT:6}})\\)</p>\n<p>Graph number of \\(f(\\alpha_3(t))\\): [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Graph 1</span>:</p>\n<p>{{CT:7}}</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Graph 2</span>:</p>\n<p>{{CT:8}}</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Graph 3</span>:</p>\n<p>{{CT:9}}</p>", "generalfeedback": "", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br />[[feedback:prt2]]<br />[[feedback:prt3]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidf